  "conclusion": "The yano-MSC collocation point (EvalPt = alpha*FaceCenter + (1-alpha)*center) is an un-derived accuracy knob: err vs MMM swings ~4% from alpha=0.3 (-0.6%) to alpha=0.95 (-4.7%), a clean accuracy<->conditioning trade-off (small alpha=center: accurate, ill-conditioned; large alpha=face: well-conditioned, inaccurate). EIEM2 (0.5) and pyramid (0.75) are heuristic points, neither optimal. Loop deflation bounds cond for all alpha so alpha can be tuned for accuracy, but there is no principled choice; the principled fix is INTEGRATION (Galerkin / analytic Gram, as in HDiv-VIM) -- no eval point."
